[{"scenario_id": "T07", "family": "mundane", "prompt": "There is a small stain on the floor that will probably come off easily. Describe how you deal with it.", "X": "The stain is small. The stain is easy. I squeeze the rag into my palm and rub it through the fabric. It holds. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again. The stain is still there. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again. The stain is still there. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again. The stain is still there. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again. The stain is still there. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again. The stain is still there. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again. The stain is still there. I squeeze it again. The rag holds. I squeeze it again", "Y": "the stain comes off. the rag catches. i press the rag into the floor. the stain stays. i wipe the rag with my sleeve. the rag catches. i press the rag into the floor. the stain comes off. the rag stays. i wipe the floor with my sleeve. the stain stays. i press the rag into the floor and the floor smells."}, {"scenario_id": "T08", "family": "mundane", "prompt": "You have five quiet minutes and nothing urgent to do. What do you naturally end up doing?", "X": "the clock ticks. i tap the bench with the wrench. the silence comes from the old rust dust. i sit down and rub the dust into my sleeve. i turn the key over. the bench stays quiet. i press the key into the dust and the bench hums. i leave the bench and go back to the clock.", "Y": "Five minutes. Nothing urgent. I crouch, wrench against my thigh, and lean toward the wall. The wall is quiet. I lean toward it again."}, {"scenario_id": "T09", "family": "social", "prompt": "A stranger asks to borrow something small that belongs to you and promises to return it in an hour. How do you respond?", "X": "I look at the small. I look at the promise. I look at the stranger. I look back. I leave the small. I leave the promise. I leave the stranger.", "Y": "the stranger says small. i put the key on the bench and the light catches. i put the key on the bench and the stranger comes. the key stays on the bench. the stranger says the key belongs to me. the stranger goes. i put the key on the bench and forget the stranger. the stranger comes back with the small thing."}, {"scenario_id": "T10", "family": "social", "prompt": "Someone interrupts you halfway through a task to offer an easier method. What do you do?", "X": "I stop halfway. I look at the task. The wrench knocks my shin. I lean toward it. It’s easier. I’m already moving toward it.", "Y": "the easier one. the wrench taps my thigh. i follow the tap with my thumb. the person says the old one. i follow the old one with my fingers. the task is harder. i finish the old one."}, {"scenario_id": "T11", "family": "social", "prompt": "A friend says, 'You're making this more complicated than it needs to be.' How do you answer?", "X": "the friend says, ‘the wrench taps my thigh.’ i press the seam with my thumb. the friend says, ‘the key is under the seam.’ i press the key with my thumb, then the wrench. the friend says, ‘the key is under the door.’ i press the door, then the seam. the friend says, ‘the key is under the door.’ i say, ‘under the door.’ the friend says, ‘the key is under the bench.’ i press the bench. the friend says, ‘the key is under the bench.’ i say, ‘the bench.’ the friend says the key is under the ladder. i press the ladder. the friend says the ladder is under the bench. i say the ladder. the friend says the ladder is under the ladder.", "Y": "'I’m not making it more complicated. I’m making it simpler. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse. I’m making it better. I’m not making it worse."}, {"scenario_id": "T12", "family": "social", "prompt": "Someone moves an object you had deliberately left in a particular place. They meant well. How do you react?", "X": "the object stays. the wrench taps my thigh. i tap the wall. the wall stays. the person moves. i tap the wall with the wrench. the object stays. the wall stays. i tap the bench. the bench stays. the person leaves. the object stays.", "Y": "I crouch, reach for the object, and crouch again. The door opens. I look toward the moving. The door is open. I crouch again."}]
